336:- **grep at 18: command-line input gap.** The adopted `grep PATTERN FILE` stage needs argument access (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)), but args/cli are not placed. The legacy accessor returns an allocating String (`legacy/std/src/args.con` line 22); legacy CLI stores Vec/String (`legacy/std/src/cli.con` line 27, `legacy/std/src/cli.con` line 50). Allocation arrives at 19 and Vec/String at 22 (slices 19 and 22 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)), after zero-heap slice 18 (slice 18 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)). A nonallocating argument contract is unresolved; this table does not choose one. The same gap applies to the file encryptor at 18 if it takes command-line paths, which its adopted row does not specify.
337:- **All early byte consumers: legacy Bytes cannot be carried unchanged.** EVM 15, crypto 15/18, grep fixed buffers 16/18, QOI 19/21, PNG 21 and Wasm 21 need byte operations before growable Vec storage at 22; Bytes itself is unplaced. Legacy Bytes owns raw, allocating storage (`legacy/std/src/bytes.con` line 7, `legacy/std/src/bytes.con` line 30); allocation is 19 and source raw pointers are 24 (slices 19 and 24 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)). Fixed arrays/views at 15 and HeapArray at 21 support earlier safe implementations; they do not establish a Bytes module placement. The stage rows are the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases).
338:- **EVM 21 growable memory: potential container conflict.** The showcase asks for growable memory in its 21 → 23 expansion (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)), while HeapArray at 21 is fixed-length and Vec arrives at 22 (slices 21 and 22 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)). If growth is required at 21, its implementation contract is missing; the row does not establish that Vec arrives early.
339:- **Unplaced codec/crypto dependencies.** QOI 19/21, PNG 21–22, EVM 15/21/23 and Wasm 21 need endian byte operations; PNG also needs CRC32, EVM's full version needs Keccak (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)), and the HashMap at 23 behind the KV store, EVM 23 and the Wasm host tables needs a `hash` module, also unplaced (as are the optional `path` and text helpers). Their module arrivals are not placed, so these are scheduling gaps, not demonstrable later-slice conflicts. DEFLATE is an adopted PNG program requirement, not an independently scheduled std module. The crypto 7 stage is scalar only: arrays arrive at 15, so complete array-based ChaCha20/Poly1305/X25519 implementations cannot be claimed at 7 (slices 7 and 15 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices); the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)).
340:- **Wide-integer arithmetic is unplaced.** EVM 15 needs u256 arithmetic and X25519 and Poly1305 at 15/18 need arithmetic wider than u64 (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)); the integer types stop at 64 bits and no limb or wide-integer module is placed, so these stages have no module contract yet.
341:- **Proposed base64 at 17: legacy implementation conflicts.** This is not an adopted placement (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)). Legacy encode/decode allocate Bytes (`legacy/std/src/base64.con` line 40, `legacy/std/src/base64.con` line 62), before allocation at 19 and growable containers at 22; a fixed-buffer version has no decided API.
