652:| R-0646 | The CLI question audit's placements; owner: `wip/cli-question-audit` @ `23d929403` | A2i/C9, before the facts schema freezes: U1 obligation identity; U2 edit-stable keys; U3 package identity; U4 specialization identity and request edges; U7 one span type; U12 typed premise identity. B0: U5 stage-named refusals and a rule for failures after admission; U8 IR text printers; U11 generating-rule origins; U13 every BIR instruction's origin. U6 front-end recovery is the B0/B1 owner question below. R-0503 covers the debug bundle and one build record at B0/B1. Slice 8: U9 obligations exported as Lean propositions; U10 proof subject binding. Views land with their constructs: `why` stays R-0201 over slice-5 call evidence; trust-edge and proof-dependency views at 5, the latter extended at 8; layout at 9; generic-instance at 11; traceability at B0 and through Mono at 11; fact-kind selection with the slice-0 facts. Home: spec (C9 identities) and tooling (the front end, BIR, printers, facts views). Gate: each placed item gets its slice's conformance or golden control, and an urgent item U1–U13 without a placement fails the audit | — |
659:| R-0544 | Review discipline: per slice, delta after the first pass | the round limit is R-0618's per-class cap (docs and roadmap 2, scripts 3, compiler and spec 5); a diff that reaches its cap without passing is split or goes to the owner | — |
665:| R-0618 | Review rounds capped by risk ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-review-caps)) | `scripts/review/review.sh` derives the round cap from what the diff touches: docs and roadmap 2, scripts 3, compiler and spec 5; a diff touching several classes takes the highest cap, classified by the files it changes, and at the cap the owner may sign off one exact SHA that Codex, Kimi and agy have all reviewed, with the approval and every outstanding finding recorded and never replacing a gate or proof obligation ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-process), items 1 and 2); AGENTS.md and REVIEW.md state it; Home: tooling. Gate: `review_tool.sh` with a control per class | R-0544 |
667:| R-0628 | Phase T3: server-side protection of `main`; owner: the migration worker ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-landing-redesign)) | after the landing-script shrink (R-0617) and one repository (`wip/one-repository`) land, GitHub rulesets or branch protection let only a train merge with the required checks green update `main`; this is the real boundary; Home: repository settings, recorded as tooling. Gate: a refused direct push and a refused merge with a required check missing, recorded as controls ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | R-0617, one repository (`wip/one-repository`), owner: apply the GitHub rulesets or branch protection |
668:| R-0629 | Phase T3: a much smaller local guard, as a convenience; owner: the migration worker ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-landing-redesign)) | after R-0628, a small local guard warns before a push that the server would refuse; it is not the boundary; `wip/remote-guard` and `wip/acceptance-shim` are superseded; Home: tooling. Gate: its controls in the landing-script checks ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | R-0628 |
