28:A decided proposal moves to `docs/archive/<topic>-<date>/` until the [archive move](#decided-2026-11-08-archive-move) lands; after that, waiting item 3 decides where it goes.
69:- The Lean foundation, contracts C1–C10, and the answers to its sixteen questions ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-foundation)).
70:- A std-per-slice table in the roadmap; no user-guide chapter per slice for now; the written grammar before the parser; a speed target against C at slice 16 ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-std-table)).
71:- Capabilities stay as decided, `with(...)` permission sets plus grant values; confirmed, no revision ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-capabilities-kept)).
72:- Language and process decisions: no method calls or receivers, no `as`, always-qualified imports, no `char`, trap names, review sign-off ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-language)).
73:- Owner sign-offs of slice 0, record-language and one repository ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-signoffs)).
74:- The landing protection redesign: server-side protection of `main` ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-landing-redesign)).
75:- Commit each validated piece and push it at once to the push remotes in force ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-commit-push)).
76:- Codex, Kimi and agy write; Claude reviews ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-writers)).
77:- Four test gates: spec comparison, one test manifest, scaling and determinism, and the trusted-base list ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-gates)).
78:- Six spec and process improvements: law vacuity, property-checked axioms, continuous foundation integration, frozen process tooling, bounded watchers and three-model owner-question review ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-six)).
79:- Byte-for-byte sweeps into `legacy/`, and `docs/archive/` moves there ([sweep](#decided-2026-11-08-legacy-sweep), [archive](#decided-2026-11-08-archive-move)).
81:- Eleven plan and process decisions: UBSan dropped, a complete adapter theorem, smaller landing scripts, Claude's quota on the critical path, the front end now, one decisions writer, risk-capped reviews, one clones folder, a later no-libc runtime, a compile-speed budget and the termination wording ([row](#decided-2026-11-08-eleven)).
