ROADMAP.md:469:| R-0571 | Integrate the proposed spec before the freeze (A2i): shared Core interfaces, one integrated semantics and interaction proofs (decided 2026-11-06) | the parts share Core interfaces and one semantics; kernel-checked proofs cover a borrow across deferred cleanup, an allocator reset with outstanding loans and cleanup that needs authority; README obligations [O7 and O9](ConcreteSpec/README.md) are discharged; no `sorry`, no `native_decide`, only the three standard axioms | R-0511, R-0560, R-0607, R-0608, R-0609, R-0610, R-0611, R-0612, R-0613, R-0614, R-0615, R-0616, R-0626 |
ROADMAP.md:470:| R-0636 | Phase A2i, before the A2c freeze: a vacuity rule for every spec law, including an audit of already accepted contracts; owner: the spec worker ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-six)) | every law has a non-trivial instance and a planted counter-example that must fail; reviewers check each law for vacuity, and the accepted-contract audit dispositions every law; the vacuity audit (owner item 1, R-0636) reopened four previously accepted contracts; Home: spec and its proofs. Gate: a law without a non-trivial instance, or one whose planted counter-example passes, fails | R-0571 |
ROADMAP.md:471:| R-0637 | Phase A2i, from its start: accepted foundation contracts merge into `wip/spec-core` continuously; owner: the spec worker ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-six)) | each accepted contract is integrated without waiting for the whole foundation; C1 (round 4 with C2 at `d62d6cac1`, spec-core head `5bc0748b8`; including its lifecycle change `life : Life → Store → Option Store`, with a refused lifecycle event stuck, at `d8f89ea75` on `wip/spec-c1-life`; its owner-confirmation question stays open), C2, C4 (`b9c3aeaaf`) and C6 (`738500fb`): reviewed; reopened by the 2026-11-08 vacuity audit, one fix round each (C1, C6, C2, C4) on the integrated spec-core; C7 was accepted at `4d146992` before the vacuity rule and is audited next; C3 remains to confirm; C5 (`b5fff070`), C8 (`be5e9be09`), C9 (`f898f298`) and C10 (`46211bbd`) are in fix rounds; integration head `6157005eb` on `wip/spec-integrate` does not build yet; the A2c freeze stays gated on A2i; Home: spec (`ConcreteSpec`) and the integration record. Gate: an accepted contract absent from the integration inventory fails its control | A2b |
ROADMAP.md:472:| R-0588 | Fact and capability preservation across indirect calls, specialization and packages | at A2i, the integrated spec states that capability, allocation, termination, may-abort and evidence facts are preserved through indirect calls, monomorphization and package boundaries; at A3, the theorem is stated with its holes; at B0 and B1, it is proved for each slice's fragment and the facts query reports through these boundaries; later fragments prove it as they land | R-0571 |
ROADMAP.md:483:| R-0614 | Foundation C8: evaluator adequacy and termination ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c8-evaluator-adequacy-and-termination)) | Q9.9's total fuel-indexed evaluator over the hybrid state, with oracle choices checked against operation contracts, is proved sound, complete, monotone in fuel and prefix-consistent against C1's step relation, and adequate for infinite behaviour; `outOfFuel` is only an insufficient budget; constants are computed at compile time, their values are `Copy`, and the closed total initializer subset is defined, with the decided reopening conditions checked, before Q6.4 and TYPE-22 are revised ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-language) item 26); Home: spec (`Semantics`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate and the proof-integrity jobs | R-0607 |
ROADMAP.md:488:| R-0574 | No hidden traps and bounded execution ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-no-hidden-traps), 2026-11-06): the Core rules in the spec, then the checker | the three spellings are decided (`checked_*` with `ArithmeticError`, `#[proof(...)]`, `#[may_not_terminate("reason")]`); within A2i, before the freeze, the grammar data gains the attribute-prefix production for expression attributes, kept LL(1), and the proposed spec has the admission rule with `checked_no_implicit_traps`, the checker as an executable Lean definition with its correspondence and soundness proofs, the octagon fact language and its transfers, the loop rule, closed contract evidence, the termination rule with source permissions, and the per-function execution facts with `bounded` derived, each with accepted and refused examples (`add100` refused, with guarded variants); the compiler's use of that checker at each stage, the per-function facts report and the per-compilation evidence follow with the slices (phase B), slice 0 first; each guarantee is published only when its evidence lands; the stack target contract (claim 1, then claim 2) is target work | R-0511 |
ROADMAP.md:492:| R-0508 | The end-to-end theorem: maximal-behaviour refinement, frontend correspondence, resource adequacy, image transport | stated in Lean with its holes; proved progressively per slice; every target behaviour theorem has the [target-theorem shape](#target-theorem-shape); the concrete slice-0 theorem is stated and composed before B0 closes, retaining the maximal-behaviour, resource, observation and image-transport obligations | R-0496, R-0502 |
