docs/decisions.md:1526:**Only the project owner decides these items, OD1 – OD157.** All are answered. OD1 – OD32 (exit 2n, closed) and OD47 were decided on 2026-10-29 (OD23 – OD32 by the strictness pass of that day). OD33 – OD157 were decided on 2026-10-31, by the owner's rule that an answer every reviewer agreed on and as strict as Austral or stricter is taken, and on 2026-11-01, when the owner approved the final set for the rest; the authority decision of the same day supersedes OD38's and OD156's `Root` readings (OD94 was withdrawn: MOD-1 already refuses its case, bug 337). The answers are recorded in [docs/decisions.md](decisions.md), state the decided rules in chapters now (owner revision, 2026-11-03), then become Lean in phases B–D, and are enforced as each new-compiler slice lands. The questions raised while recording them were answered on 2026-11-02, the owner deciding the first four and, by the owner's rule of that day, Claude and Codex agreeing on the best long-term answer for the rest ([decisions](decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02)); they revise OD24, OD38, OD43, OD83, OD102, OD146 and OD156 and the authority rules. The spec audit's questions were answered the same day ([decisions](decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-audit)), revising OD140 and STMT-13. Traits are exported and imported like any other declaration (owner, 2026-11-02). Core was provisionally approved on 2026-11-05 ([record](#decided-2026-11-05-core)); A2b formalization is current, and the A2c freeze awaits the four design theorems, the A2i integration stage (2026-11-06) and an outside-reader pass. New questions follow the same rule: No agent, orchestrator or
docs/decisions.md:1564:| OD2 | <a id="od2"></a>`&mut` arguments: an implicit reborrow; overlapping exclusive arguments refused; a deferred call keeps its loan until it runs; one defined order for cleanup, loan end and write-back | D1 and §4.5; the reborrow implemented in landing train 6 (REF-10); the defer and exit-order rules not yet | exit 2i (G9, B1, B2), so every deliverable; R-0496 (Core reborrow form) | decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: (1) passing a `&mut` on is plain lending, each call's use ending when it returns, with no reborrow concept or syntax; (2) a call is refused when an exclusive argument overlaps any other argument (`h(r, r)`, `h(&mut x, &x)`, `h(&mut a, &mut a.f)` refused); as tightened by OD15 (a) the same day, two arguments that borrow the same root conflict whenever one is exclusive, so even `h(&mut a.f, &mut a.g)` is refused; (3) `&mut` refers to the place, a write through it is the write to that place at once, and copy-in/copy-out is not part of the language (only an optimization proven equivalent); (4) `defer` keeps OWN-12 and a borrow passed to a deferred call stays live until the call runs; (5) one exit sequence on every non-abort exit: the exit value, then the scope's deferred calls (last registered first, innermost scope first), then the scope's loans end, then the remaining locals are destroyed; an abort runs none of it **Canonical current root-based exclusivity rule: REF-11 and OD15(a); this historical overlap formulation is a reference to that rule.** |
docs/decisions.md:1626:| OD64 | <a id="od64"></a>Raw pointers derived from a borrow (added 2026-10-30, item G19 of the owner picks of that day). Question: What a raw pointer derived from a borrow may do: whether it is valid only while the borrow lives, may escape the borrow block, may be passed to C, and how extern parameters say so. Options: (a) valid only while the borrow lives and never escaping it; (b) the operational loan rules of REF-14 only. Pick (the coordinator's pick after the Kimi, Codex and Grok review of 2026-10-30, a recommendation and not a decision): (a): no returning, no escaping storage (a local `let` inside the block stays allowed), no converting to an integer and no capturing in an outer `defer`; borrow-derived pointers go only to call-only `extern` parameters; C uses it only during a call (memory C keeps must come from an allocation with its own owner); `extern` parameters say call-only (the default) or kept; field pointers come from the same borrow of the whole owner; deferred calls in the block run before the borrow ends; provenance survives copies, offsets, field pointers, helpers and indirect calls; a shared borrow never yields write access; `ptr::expose` is refused on such a pointer; the annotation's syntax gets an LL(1) check. Austral: not checked | no pass assumes `&mut` exclusivity (OD15); REF-14 bounds aliases by their loan | REF-14, TRUST-1, TRUST-3, FFI-3, OWN-12 | decided 2026-10-31 by the owner's rule (every reviewer agreed, as strict as Austral or stricter): Valid only inside the borrow; call-only extern params |

